== params: SQL and Params wiring
ok ParamCheck is True by default
ok ReadOnly is False by default
ok no parameters without SQL
ok assigning SQL builds the parameters, one per name
ok changing SQL rebuilds them in the order of first occurrence
ok a parameter that occurs again keeps its value
ok every change of the lines is parsed; literals and comments are skipped
ok ParamByName is case-insensitive
ok ParamByName of a missing name
ok with ParamCheck False the parameters are left alone
ok SQL without parameters clears them
ok the query opens
ok and is prepared
ok changing SQL closes an active dataset
ok and unprepares
ok the new statement runs at the next Open
== prepare
ok Prepare without a connection
ok Open without a connection
ok ExecSQL without a connection
ok not prepared at first
ok the connection is closed
ok Prepare opens a closed connection
ok Prepared after Prepare
ok Prepare does not open the dataset
ok Prepare again is a no-op
ok Unprepare finalizes
ok Unprepare again is a no-op
ok Prepared := True prepares
ok Prepared := False unprepares
ok empty SQL
ok comment-only SQL
ok Open with empty SQL
ok the dataset stays closed
ok two statements
ok nothing stays prepared
ok a terminating semicolon and white space are allowed
ok a positional parameter
ok a numbered parameter
ok nothing stays prepared after it
ok a syntax error
ok its primary code
ok its SQL is the statement text
ok the error is an ESQLiteError
ok Open of an unknown table
ok Open prepares implicitly
ok closing the dataset keeps the statement prepared
ok the prepared statement is used again
ok closing the connection closes the dataset
ok and unprepares
ok Open opens the connection again
ok and runs the statement
== binding
ok an unbound parameter is NULL
ok AsInteger
ok a negative integer
ok AsLargeInt
ok AsFloat
ok an integral float stays REAL
ok AsBoolean True
ok AsBoolean False
ok AsString
ok an empty string is empty TEXT, not NULL
ok non-ASCII text
ok comes back unchanged
ok AsBytes
ok empty bytes are an empty BLOB, not NULL
ok AsDateTime
ok AsDateTime with milliseconds
ok a year below 1000 has four digits
ok a cleared parameter is NULL
ok an embedded #0 does not cut a text value
ok and the text comes back unchanged
ok only the :name form is parsed
ok the @name and $name forms are bound by name too
ok names differing in case are one parameter
ok and every spelling is bound
ok a statement parameter without a TParam
ok the dataset stays closed
ok the same in ExecSQL
ok first execution
ok changing a parameter does not touch the open dataset
ok Refresh binds the current values
ok and so does the next Open
ok an unbound parameter replaces the earlier binding by NULL
== exec
ok RowsAffected is -1 before any ExecSQL
ok a CREATE TABLE changes no rows
ok ExecSQL prepares implicitly
ok and does not open the dataset
ok an INSERT of one row
ok the prepared statement ran once per ExecSQL with the values of that call
ok an UPDATE of three rows
ok a CREATE TABLE after it does not repeat the count
ok a DELETE that matches nothing
ok ExecSQL of a SELECT ignores the rows
ok and the dataset stays closed
ok a DELETE of one row
ok the same DELETE again finds nothing
ok a constraint error in ExecSQL
ok the statement is usable after the error
ok and the connection too
ok ExecSQL on an active dataset
ok the dataset stays open
== result sets
ok Open of a statement without columns
ok the dataset stays closed
ok and the statement did not run
ok duplicate column names get suffixes in column order
ok and keep their values
ok a suffixed name that exists is a duplicate itself
ok empty column names become Column<N>
ok the columns of a join
ok with their values
ok all rows are fetched at Open
ok in statement order
ok a later change of the table does not reach the open dataset
ok Refresh runs the statement again
ok and so does closing and opening
ok Unprepare leaves an open dataset open
ok Refresh prepares the statement again
ok no statement stays active after Open: the table can be dropped, the rows stay
ok two thousand rows are all in memory
ok up to the last one
== errors while loading
ok an SQLite error at the second row
ok the dataset does not become active
ok and has no fields
ok the statement was reset: it runs after the data is repaired
ok a convert error at the second row
ok the dataset does not become active
ok the statement was reset: the table can be dropped
ok an SQLite error in Refresh propagates
ok the dataset stays open
ok and the statement was reset
== field definitions of a closed query
ok FieldDefs.Update leaves the dataset closed
ok and builds the definitions
ok with their names
ok and sizes
ok no statement stays active after it
ok FieldDefs.Update reports the errors of the statement
== connection
ok changing Connection on an active dataset
ok the connection is unchanged
ok the query is registered with its connection
ok changing Connection unprepares
ok the query left the old connection
ok and is registered with the new one
ok the new connection is opened by Open
ok destroying the connection closes the dataset
ok and clears Connection
ok a destroyed query leaves its connection
